            "review_title": "Review at Hai San Bien Dong",
            "review_text": "Roved\nSydney, Australia121 contributions\n0\nWhat a great place!\nFeb 2020 • Couples\nWhat a great restaurant, and a great Vietnamese experience!! We ate here both nights of our stay in Can Tho - our meal the first night was so good and other options in Can Tho did not appeal(although lunch at Spicer’s at Victoria superb! But full of tour groups in evening.) The seafood here is fresh, and perfectly cooked. We ate fabulous grilled prawns, lightly fried tender baby squid, clams, brilliant scallops (over the two nights!). Morning glory the best we’ve had. Yes, no English is spoken and menu only in Vietnamese, but the staff could not have been more helpful and this is exactly what google translate is for!! Sure, avoid if you are a fussy eater or want to spend your Vietnamese holiday eating European food with other foreigners. But you’re in Vietnam, after all! Highly recommend this very authentic restaurant!\nRead more\nWritten February 11, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
