            "review_text": "Ernest C\nSingapore, Singapore200 contributions\n0\nBest seafood , tamarind crab is fabulous !!!\nMay 2017 • Business\nFinally visited Can Tho city having been traveling in Vietnam for the past 20 years. Can Tho and the surrounding Mekong Delta is the country's largest producer of agricultural and seafood products. Come dinner time , the hotel staff recommended seafood which is probably the safest bet in a city where choices are few and far between. There are apparently 2 branches in the city , and I ended up eating at both on 2 consecutive days. The seafood is simply fabulous and out of this world. What is truly worth highlighting is the Tamarind crab (\"Cua Rang Me\") , grilled squid and flower-like vegetables. I am a crab lover and has eaten tamarind crabs many times in Ho Chi Minh city but this is the BEST that I have eaten to date. The crabs are very fresh and full of roe , and the tamarind sauce is very well balanced and blended perfectly with the crabs. The same can be said of the rest of the items , fresh ingredients that retain its original flavor. This is a restaurant that I will highly recommend for anyone looking for a good venue for dinner. Don't forget the local Vietnamese fried rice with crispy silver fish which should be a good complement to a full satisfactory meal in Can Tho City. The prices are very reasonable from a tourist's perspective although many may consider to be on a higher side for a provincial city in Vietnam.\nRead more\nWritten May 18, 2017",
